✔ Copy directory                    -r   Use -r for directories
✔ Best for backup                   -a   Always use -a for backups
✔ Preserve attributes               -a
✔ Ask before overwriting              -i
✔ Show progress                     -v
✔ Copy only newer files             -u
✔ Contents only → /.
✔ Hidden files → never use * alone

===========================================================================================================================

Q.1> Copy /etc/hosts to /root/hosts.bak and keep all attributes.

A.1> cp -p /etc/hosts /root/hosts.bak

-p preserves permissions, ownership, and timestamps.

===========================================================================================================================

Q.2> Copy /var/log to /backup/log.

A.2> cp -r /var/log /backup/log

Directories require -r or -R.

===========================================================================================================================

Q.3> Create an exact backup of /etc to /backup/etc.

A.3> cp -a /etc /backup/etc

-a (archive) preserves:
permissions
ownership
timestamps
symlinks

==========================================================================================================================

Q.4> Create a backup of /etc in /backup/etc preserving all file attributes.

A.4> cp -a /etc /backup/etc

===========================================================================================================================

Q.5> Copy the file /var/log/messages to /root/messages.bak and keep permissions and ownership.

A.5> cp -p /var/log/messages /root/messages.bak

===========================================================================================================================

Q.6> Copy all files from /data to /archive/data without copying the directory itself.

A.6> cp -a /data/. /archive/data/

============================================================================================================================

Q.7> Copy the directory /opt/scripts to /mnt/scripts and show each copied file on the terminal.

A.7> cp -av /opt/scripts /mnt/scripts

==========================================================================================================================

Q.8> Copy all .conf files from /etc to /tmp/conf_backup.

A.8> cp /etc/*.conf /tmp/conf_backup/

===========================================================================================================================

Q.9> Copy /home/user1 to /backup/user1 so that symbolic links are preserved.

A.9> cp -a /home/user1 /backup/user1

===========================================================================================================================

Q.10> Copy files from /source to /destination only if the source files are newer.

A.10> cp -ru /source/. /destination/

=========================================================================================================================

Q.11> Copy the file report.txt to /data but prompt before overwriting an existing file.

A.11> cp -i report.txt /data/

==========================================================================================================================

Q.12> Copy all files (including hidden files) from /project to /backup/project.

A.12> cp -a /project/. /backup/project/

==============================================================================================================================

